proof: discimagecreator | opensuse | vendor-cap
date: 2026-07-15
lane/VM: test-openSUSE (Leap 16.0, autologin Plasma X11 -> seat0), OBS repo
user groups: "gmipf wheel" (NO cdrom/disk/plugdev) -> groupless
drive: PLEXTOR PX-760A (USB) -> /dev/sr1
mechanism: openSUSE permissions framework (permissions.d/discimagecreator + permctl)

Note: DIC pre-checks free space and aborts if the output dir is too small. openSUSE
/tmp is a 1 GB tmpfs -> DIC bailed ("not enough disk space"). Re-run with output in
~ (27 GB free) so DIC actually performs the D8 dump. Not a cap issue.

--- delivery ---
$ /usr/sbin/getcap /usr/libexec/discimagecreator/DiscImageCreator.out -> cap_sys_rawio=ep
  (DVDAuth.out also carries it)
$ rpm -qf DiscImageCreator.out -> discimagecreator-20260703121302.efa7d482-lp160.26.1

--- GREEN (cap present, output in ~/dicg) ---
$ discimagecreator cd /dev/sr1 ~/dicg/t.bin 8 /d8
  supports [OpCode: 0xd8, SubCode: 0/1/...]   (4 hits)
  Creating (Lead-in)...                       # D8 lead-in read
  permit-errors: 0

--- RED (setcap -r, then restored) ---
$ /usr/sbin/setcap -r .../DiscImageCreator.out ; getcap -> []
$ discimagecreator cd /dev/sr1 ~/dicr/t.bin 8 /d8
  lpCmd: d8, ...        (0xd8 CDB sent 6x)
  [F:ExecSearchingOffset] / [F:ReadCDForCheckingSubPack] / [F:ReadEeprom]
     GetLastError: 1, Operation not permitted   (7 permit-errors)
$ /usr/sbin/setcap cap_sys_rawio=ep .../DiscImageCreator.out -> cap restored

VERDICT: PROVEN. permctl-delivered cap is load-bearing: with it the 0xd8 vendor CDBs
(and Plextor ReadEeprom) reach the drive; without it they EPERM (kernel gate).
